/- English proof (translation)
Use `⟨0, fun _ _ _ => ⟨0, fun D _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ ch _ _ => ?_⟩⟩` and prove the remaining obligations. Introduce `t M hM X hX _`. Use `(hM.vtx X ?_).haar_fund` and prove the remaining obligations. Apply the tactic sequence `cases X <;> simp only [DefNode, Node.InRange] at hX ⊢ <;> omega`.
-/
theorem c3 : Big fun ch => ∀ t (M : Vol ch.G), M.Is t → IsHaarDef M := by
  refine ⟨0, fun _ _ _ => ⟨0, fun D _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ ch _ _ => ?_⟩⟩
  intro t M hM X hX _
  refine (hM.vtx X ?_).haar_fund
  cases X <;> simp only [DefNode, Node.InRange] at hX ⊢ <;> omega

/- English proof (translation)
Use `⟨0, fun _ _ _ => ⟨0, fun D _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ ch _ _ => ?_⟩⟩` and prove the remaining obligations. Introduce `t Φ β M hM X hX hne`. Consider the cases of `X with`. Consider the case `grid i j`. Take `⟨hi, rfl⟩` from `hX`.

Conclude with `(hM.2 i hi).haar_fund`. Consider the case `top j`. Establish `: j < D.R.m` using `lt_of_le_of_ne hX (fun e => hne (by rw [e]))`. Conclude with `(hM.1 j this).haar_fund`. Consider the case `core i => exact hX.elim`.
-/
theorem c4 : Big fun ch => ∀ t Φ β M, IsTermVol t ch.S.toGridChoice Φ β M → IsHaarDef M := by
  refine ⟨0, fun _ _ _ => ⟨0, fun D _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ ch _ _ => ?_⟩⟩
  intro t Φ β M hM X hX hne
  cases X with
  | grid i j =>
    obtain ⟨hi, rfl⟩ := hX
    exact (hM.2 i hi).haar_fund
  | top j =>
    have : j < D.R.m := lt_of_le_of_ne hX (fun e => hne (by rw [e]))
    exact (hM.1 j this).haar_fund
  | core i => exact hX.elim

/- English proof (translation)
Establish `hall` using `(((((((GlobalTheory.T.besselColumnScalarFunction_continuous_leftInvariant.and GlobalTheory.T.gridTopVertexFormFunction_continuous_left_invariant).and c3).and c4).and GlobalTheory.T.unfoldingJointData_jointlySmoothTheta_evenIndex).and GlobalTheory.T.rowTest_flippedFiniteTensor_row …`. Use `GlobalTheory.RowReal.big_mono (fun ch h => ?_) hall` and prove the remaining obligations. Break down `h with ⟨⟨⟨⟨⟨⟨⟨h1, h2⟩, h3⟩, h4⟩, h5a⟩, h5b⟩, h6⟩, h7⟩` into its components or cases. Use `⟨fun a => ⟨(h1 a).2, (h1 a).1⟩, fun t y => ⟨(h2 t y).2, (h2 t y).1⟩, h3, h4, ?_, h6, h7⟩` and prove the remaining obligations. Introduce `t Φ τ hτ M hM d hd P hh`.

Conclude with `⟨fun j hj hjm => h5a t Φ τ hτ M hM d hd P hh j hj hjm, h5b t Φ τ hτ d hd⟩`.
-/
theorem basicAt : Big fun ch => BasicAt ch := by
  have hall := (((((((GlobalTheory.T.besselColumnScalarFunction_continuous_leftInvariant.and GlobalTheory.T.gridTopVertexFormFunction_continuous_left_invariant).and c3).and c4).and GlobalTheory.T.unfoldingJointData_jointlySmoothTheta_evenIndex).and GlobalTheory.T.rowTest_flippedFiniteTensor_row_isThetaFunction).and GlobalTheory.T.rowTest_heisenberg_combinations_joint_row_good).and GlobalTheory.T.rowTest_exists_combinations_of_expansion)
  refine GlobalTheory.RowReal.big_mono (fun ch h => ?_) hall
  rcases h with ⟨⟨⟨⟨⟨⟨⟨h1, h2⟩, h3⟩, h4⟩, h5a⟩, h5b⟩, h6⟩, h7⟩
  refine ⟨fun a => ⟨(h1 a).2, (h1 a).1⟩, fun t y => ⟨(h2 t y).2, (h2 t y).1⟩, h3, h4, ?_, h6, h7⟩
  intro t Φ τ hτ M hM d hd P hh
  exact ⟨fun j hj hjm => h5a t Φ τ hτ M hM d hd P hh j hj hjm, h5b t Φ τ hτ d hd⟩

